<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen down on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen down on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's gold prices are likely to slip further this week in line with world gold prices and a depressed demand in the domestic market, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The gold demand has lowered in the past few months because of Pakistan's weak economic conditions,&quot; dealer Farooq Qureshi said. &quot;Falling gold rates abroad also affect the local market.&quot;</p>
<p>    Weekly prices:				 Monday	July 28</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams   4,385	 4,406</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grams		     6,000	 6,000</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
